## Step 2 — implement
This bead is an enumeration-closure job, and the failure mode is silence: a
missed column list makes the lease read back as nil, which compiles clean and
passes tests that do not look for it. Work the `pinned` precedent method the
bead's Contract spells out (migration 023 added `pinned` exactly this way), and
treat the bead's counterpart counts as a floor, not a target.

Two boundaries your Contract already fixes — respect them exactly:
- `internal/storage/sqlite/queries.go`: you own the `SearchIssues` SELECT list
  (:1644) because it delegates to the shared `scanIssues` you are changing. The
  storage-core bead deliberately left it alone. `internal/storage/sqlite/labels.go`
  `GetIssuesByLabel` (:156-166) is the same case and is in your Touches.
- The recursive dep-tree CTE queries in `dependencies.go` (around :512 and :553)
  stay UNCHANGED: their column lists are deliberately partial, carry no late
  columns at all, and their scanners expect exactly those columns. Adding the
  lease there produces a runtime Scan error.

Every SELECT list you extend needs its scanner extended in the same edit, or the
package stops compiling on a column-count mismatch.

## Step 3 — gate and close, in this order
1. `bdc test <the files you changed>`
2. every `## Acceptance` command in the bead, in the bead's order, each exiting 0
3. `bdc <bead-id> <the files you changed>` — this runs the gate, makes the
   tagged pathspec commit, and closes the bead. It does not push; do not push.

The repo's gate command is already configured in the tracked `.bdc.conf` at the
worktree root. Do not create, edit, or delete that file.

